<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patriarch Nikon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1605">1605</a>–1681</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Nikon of Moscow</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikon was Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> from 1652 to 1666. A close adviser of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Alexis, he reformed Russian liturgical books and rituals to bring them into line with contemporary Greek practice, ordering for example the sign of the cross with three fingers rather than two. Opposition to the reforms produced the schism of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-believers">Old Believers</a>, and his claims for church authority against the tsar led to his deposition by a church council in 1666.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patriarch-nikon.jpg" alt="Patriarch Nikon" width="320" height="625" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bezmin, Ivan Artemyev · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikon_by_Ivan_Bezmin_(1680s,_Kremlin_museum).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 1650s the liturgical reforms of <b>Patriarch Nikon</b> split the church: the Old Believers who rejected them were condemned in 1666–1667, and their leader Avvakum was burned in 1682.</blockquote><a href="/empire/tsardom-of-russia">Tsardom of Russia · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Old Russian church architecture, with its many domes and wooden forms, drew on pre-Christian building, and some scholars find early Slavic ideas among the Old Believers who split from the church after <b>Patriarch Nikon</b>’s reform of 1656.</blockquote><a href="/religion/slavic-paganism">Slavic paganism · Legacy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Veldemanovo, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslavl">Yaroslavl</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=55.66,44.65&amp;year=1654" aria-label="Veldemanovo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5524 266 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Patriarch Nikon"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5974 536h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5974 536h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=55.66,44.65&amp;year=1654">What was here in 1654? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
